cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this software in academic or derivative work, please cite this repository.
  This is an open scholarly verification pipeline; reuse and extension are permitted
  with attribution.

title: "Geometric Occupancy Rule — Canonical Anchor Fit (GOR-CAF)"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2025-12-20"

authors:
  - family-names: Wells
    given-names: "A. R."
    affiliation: "Dual-Frame Research Group"

repository-code: "https://github.com/arwells-research/gor-caf"
license: MIT

keywords:
  - atomic ionization energies
  - periodic table
  - geometric occupancy rule
  - canonical anchor fit
  - baseline robustness
  - verification pipeline
  - NIST data
  - reproducible analysis

abstract: >-
  A verification-grade analysis pipeline for the Geometric Occupancy Rule (GOR),
  implementing the Canonical Anchor Fit (CAF) and baseline-holdout diagnostics
  to test invariant mid-shell structure in p-block ionization energies
  across Periods 2–5 using raw NIST data.

notes: >-
  This repository provides verification operators and robustness diagnostics only.
  It does not perform chemical fitting or many-body modeling.
